"""Autonomous, readable report for the frozen exploratory Bayesian benchmark."""
from .common import *
import shutil

def fmt(x,n=5):return '—' if x is None else f'{x:.{n}f}'
def render(state,reason):
 a=read(OUT/'analysis.json') if (OUT/'analysis.json').exists() else None;c=read(OUT/'completion.json') if (OUT/'completion.json').exists() else None
 text=f'# Learned Bayesian deck inference with baseline A allocation\n\nState: **{state}**. Updated {iso()}.\n\n{reason}\n\n'
 text+='This is an exploratory development benchmark on296 existing BO3 histories:37 exact lists × eight histories, balanced by initial chooser. The intended pool is30 passing lists representing82/100 snapshot entries; full-field reporting retains all37 lists and n/100 weights. Every list has60 cards. No new matches, held-out access, neural training, GPU, PPO, policy changes, uploads, submissions or paid model APIs are authorized. Historical evidence remains unchanged.\n\n'
 text+='## Literature adaptation and model\n\nEger and Sauma Chacón’s [Deck Archetype Prediction in Hearthstone](historical-reference-omitted), Section5.2, combines per-card observation probabilities with class prevalence under a conditional-independence approximation. This experiment adapts that idea to exact deck lists and accumulated legal revelations across BO3; it does not reproduce their first-turn Hearthstone classification experiment.\n\n'
 text+='For each training BO3, the observation ledger counts legally established physical copies once per game and retains the maximum justified count across games. It does not sum overlapping prefixes or count the same recovered copy twice. The statistical fit sums one final ledger per training BO3. For deckd/cardc, theta=(training reveal count+alpha×deck copies/60)/(total training reveals+alpha). Candidate log weights are log(prevalence)+beta×sum(revealed lower bound×log(theta)); hard compatibility is identical to A and normalization uses stable log arithmetic. This is an approximate reveal-frequency classifier, not an exact history posterior or a policy-action likelihood model. Only legal card-copy lower bounds enter classifier inference.\n\n'
 text+='The four outer folds each contain one chooser and one non-chooser BO3 per list. Each outer model fits six histories/list; three inner folds each validate two/list and train four/list. Alpha∈{30,120}, beta∈{.25,.5,1}. Selection minimizes BO3-averaged inner deck log loss under n/100 weighting. Ties within1e-12 prefer lower beta, then higher alpha. Outer labels/scores do not select parameters. Every evaluation prediction is out-of-fold. Fixed library/prevalence are shared; beta0 is baselineA.\n\n'
 text+='## Shared observation and allocation correctness\n\nThe initial all-history gate failed25 histories. The isolated shared source was repaired using native SDK semantics: Metang86 attaches Metal Energy from Looking during its verified LookDeck4 segment; Dwebble344’s Ascension attack478 evolves from Deck. Both source fixes apply identically to A, B and the diagnostic. Failed gate records are retained. The repaired fact layer processes all296 histories, checks certified facts against separate labels, and passes deduplication/copy/reset checks. All17,029 registered selected points pass A’s ordering-support flag. Eleven histories retain PF-specific typed-compiler unsupported selection profiles; the Bayesian/A method does not use that particle/action-history compiler. These remain disclosed rather than being described as universal SDK support.\n\n'
 if (OUT/'correctness-gate.json').exists():text+=f'Focused prelaunch tests: **{read(OUT/"correctness-gate.json")["tests_passed"]} passed**. Exact physical-permutation references check allocation means and variances, Basic opening predicates, ambiguous known copies and hidden Basic slots; tests also cover the Bayesian formula, stable zeros, total variance, grouped balanced folds, deduplication and leakage boundaries.\n\n'
 text+='At every selected point, common legal processing computes A’s conditional presence/count estimates once per supported deck. A mixes them using compatibility-filtered prevalence; B changes only those weights. Conditional allocation means preserve A’s existing assumptions. The feature output includes additional-unknown-copy hand presence, expected unknown hand/draw/prize counts and all three count variances. Total expected hand count is unknown mean plus the retained certified known-hand count. Mixtures use E[conditional variance]+variance of conditional means. No neural location model, particles or historical trajectory reconstruction are used.\n\n'
 text+='A separately labelled known-deck diagnostic selects the true list’s already-computed conditional output in the scorer, after legal A/B predictions have been produced. Neither candidate weights nor allocation inference receives the true index or hidden labels. The diagnostic is not deployable and is not guaranteed to be an accuracy upper bound.\n\n'
 text+='## Evaluation, uncertainty and limits\n\nThe existing queries and exact selected indices are preserved. Uncertain queries are fixed by A∈[.10,.90]. Aggregation is queries→decisions→games→BO3→equal chooser→n/82 or n/100. Paired20,000 whole-BO3 bootstrap draws use the same sampled histories across methods within list/chooser strata. Candidate-minus-A is reported directly: negative Brier/log-loss/count-error differences are better, positive accuracy/true-probability differences are better. Intervals condition on fitted CV models and do not capture full retraining uncertainty. The corpus was already used for development, so these are not untouched-test claims.\n\n'
 text+='Remaining-composition error compares the inferred original-deck copies still unaccounted for by the certified reveal lower bound against the true list’s remaining copies, averaged across the frozen library vocabulary. It isolates deck composition under the same evidence. Game/stage summaries are descriptive; game-three participation depends on previous outcomes. Missing scores keep their expected denominators and population coverage. A shared allocation/correctness failure stops comparative scoring; no replacements are issued.\n\n'
 text+='Execution caps:8 CPU-core hours including workers, fitting, controller and analysis;8 UTC elapsed hours from launch; four workers, one compute thread each. Workers have1GiB address-space limits,30s update and10s allocation/readout CPU guards; exact allocation enumeration retains4096-node bounds. Output is capped at2GiB and180s is reserved within both runtime caps for finalization/reporting. Budget exhaustion is explicit, with no extension or automatic follow-up. No power-plan change or sleep inhibition is required.\n\n'
 selections=[read(p) for p in sorted((OUT/'model-selection').glob('*.json'))]
 if selections:
  text+='## Inner-selected parameters\n\n| Outer fold | Alpha | Beta | Mean inner deck log loss | Training/excluded BO3 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
  for row in selections:
   selected=next(x for x in row['grid'] if x['alpha']==row['alpha'] and x['beta']==row['beta']);text+=f'| {row["outer_fold"]} | {row["alpha"]} | {row["beta"]} | {fmt(selected["inner_log_loss"])} | {len(row["training_ids"])}/{len(row["excluded_ids"])} |\n'
  text+='\nThe full grid, training IDs, excluded IDs and private model hashes are retained in model-selection/.\n\n'
 if a:
  text+='## Frozen results\n\nExpected/attempted/completed/scored BO3:296/'+str(c.get('evaluation_attempted',0) if c else len(list((OUT/'evaluation-results').glob('*.json'))))+'/'+str(a['scores_completed'])+'/'+str(a['scores_completed'])+'. Selected decisions scored: '+str(a['scored_points'])+'/'+str(a['expected_points'])+'. Complete population strata: '+str(a['all_strata_complete'])+'.\n\n'
  for pop in ('eligible','full_field'):
   pt=a['point'][pop];ci=a['CI95'][pop];cov=a['population_weight_coverage'][pop];text+=f'### {pop}: '+('n/82' if pop=='eligible' else 'n/100')+'\n\n| Method | Uncertain Brier | All Brier | ECE | Hand/draw/prize MAE | Primary population coverage |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n'
   for m in ('A','B','known_deck_diagnostic'):
    pre=m+'/all_in/';key=pre+'uncertain/prediction/brier';mae='/'.join(fmt(pt.get(pre+'all/prediction/'+k)) for k in ('hand_MAE','deck_MAE','prize_MAE'));text+=f'| {m} | {fmt(pt.get(key))} | {fmt(pt.get(pre+"all/prediction/brier"))} | {fmt(pt.get(pre+"all/prediction/ECE"))} | {mae} | {fmt(cov.get(key),3)} |\n'
   text+='\n| Legal method | Deck log loss | Multiclass Brier | True-deck probability | Top1 accuracy | Remaining-composition MAE |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
   for m in ('A','B'):text+='| '+m+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(pt.get(m+'/deck/'+k)) for k in ('log_loss','Brier','true_probability','top1_accuracy','remaining_composition_MAE'))+' |\n'
   text+='\n| Paired candidate-minus-A contrast | Point difference |95% interval |\n|---|---:|---|\n'
   for key in ('B_minus_A/all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier','B_minus_A/all_in/all/prediction/brier','B_minus_A/deck/log_loss','B_minus_A/deck/Brier','B_minus_A/deck/true_probability','B_minus_A/deck/top1_accuracy','B_minus_A/deck/remaining_composition_MAE','known_deck_diagnostic_minus_A/all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier'):text+=f'| {key} | {fmt(pt.get(key))} | {ci.get(key)} |\n'
   text+='\n'
  text+='### Game/stage breakdowns\n\n| Group / population | A uncertain Brier | B uncertain Brier | Known-deck diagnostic | Scored histories | Primary population coverage |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
  for group,entry in a['breakdowns'].items():
   for pop,table in entry.items():
    vals=table['point'];cv=table['coverage']['B'];text+=f'| {group}/{pop} | '+ ' | '.join(fmt(vals[m].get('all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier')) for m in ('A','B','known_deck_diagnostic'))+f' | {cv["histories"]} | {fmt(cv["primary_population_weight"],3)} |\n'
  text+='\n### Every deck\n\n| List/family/group | Completed | A/B/diagnostic uncertain Brier | A/B deck log loss | A/B top1 accuracy |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|\n'
  for row in a['per_deck']:
   mm=row['methods'];text+=f'| {row["deck"][:10]} {row["archetype"]} ({row["group"]}) | {row["completed"]}/8 | '+' / '.join(fmt(mm[m].get('all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier')) for m in ('A','B','known_deck_diagnostic'))+' | '+' / '.join(fmt(mm[m].get('deck/log_loss')) for m in ('A','B'))+' | '+' / '.join(fmt(mm[m].get('deck/top1_accuracy')) for m in ('A','B'))+' |\n'
  text+='\n## Costs\n\n';co=a['costs'];text+=f'Statistical fitting/inner validation: {co["statistical_fitting_inner_validation_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s. Common observer/allocation: {co["common_observer_allocation_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s. A weight/readout work: {co["A_incremental_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s; B weight/readout work: {co["B_incremental_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s. Scoring/export: {co["scoring_export_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s. These are components of one offline experiment, not three separate deployed runs.\n\n'
  if 'A_complete_CPU_seconds_per_BO3' in co:
   text+=f'Complete A system: {co["A_complete_CPU_seconds_per_BO3"]:.3f} CPU s/BO3; complete B: {co["B_complete_CPU_seconds_per_BO3"]:.3f} CPU s/BO3, each including the same common pass. Model fitting is reported separately as an upfront cost. Recurring overhead is not compared with A’s complete cost. Worker peak RSS: {fmt(co["peak_worker_RSS_MiB"],1)}MiB; this is not aggregate simultaneous memory.\n\n'
   for name in ('common_update_CPU_p50_p95','common_allocation_CPU_p50_p95','A_weight_and_mixture_CPU_p50_p95','B_weight_and_mixture_CPU_p50_p95'):text+=f'- {name} (seconds): {co.get(name)}.\n'
  pt=a['point']['eligible'];ci=a['CI95']['eligible'];bk='B_minus_A/all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier';dk='B_minus_A/deck/log_loss';hand=pt.get(bk);deck=pt.get(dk)
  if state!='COMPLETE' or not a['all_strata_complete'] or not a.get('primary_population_complete',False):decision='Outcome4: coverage insufficient or execution incomplete; no population-wide improvement claim.'
  elif hand is not None and deck is not None and ci.get(bk,[0,1])[1]<0 and ci.get(dk,[0,1])[1]<0:decision='Outcome1: deck identification and hidden-card prediction improve on this exploratory development comparison.'
  elif deck is not None and ci.get(dk,[0,1])[1]<0:decision='Outcome2: deck identification improves, but improved hidden-card prediction is not established.'
  elif hand is not None and deck is not None and hand>=0 and deck>=0:decision='Outcome3: neither primary hidden-card prediction nor deck log loss improves on the point estimates.'
  else:decision='Outcome4: evidence is inconclusive; point estimates and paired intervals do not establish both improvements.'
  text+='\n## Decision\n\n'+decision+'\n\n'
  if hand is not None:text+=f'Primary eligible-pool Brier difference: {hand:+.6f}; practical improvement magnitude {-hand:+.6f}. A0.005 reduction is a descriptive practical reference, not a substituted statistical gate. Pair it with the reported confidence interval and recurring CPU overhead.\n\n'
  oracle=pt.get('known_deck_diagnostic_minus_A/all_in/uncertain/prediction/brier');text+=f'Known-deck diagnostic minus A: {fmt(oracle)}. '
  if oracle is not None and oracle<-.005:text+='Knowing the exact list offers material downstream potential under the allocation assumptions; identification remains a plausible research priority.'
  else:text+='Knowing the exact list does not show a large average downstream gain here; conditional allocation assumptions/calibration may matter more than further classifier complexity.'
  text+=' This is a scorer-only diagnostic, not proof of an achievable upper bound. No automatic PPO, held-out evaluation or additional data collection follows.\n\n'
 failures=collections.Counter()
 for path in (OUT/'common-results').glob('*.json'):
  rr=read(path)
  if rr.get('error'):failures[rr['error']['type']+': '+rr['error']['message'][:160]]+=1
 if failures:text+='## Shared failures\n\n'+str(dict(failures))+'\n\nClassifier comparison is unavailable when shared allocation correctness is unresolved; failed and in-flight inputs remain retained.\n\n'
 if c:text+=f'Execution before final report: {c.get("elapsed_seconds",0)/3600:.3f} UTC hours and {c.get("aggregate_CPU_seconds",0)/3600:.3f} CPU-core hours; final totals in completion.json. Common attempted/completed/failed: {c.get("common_attempted",0)}/{c.get("common_completed",0)}/{c.get("common_failed",0)}. Private output {c.get("private_bytes",0)/1024**2:.2f}MiB.\n\n'
 if (OUT/'preparation-costs.json').exists():
  p=read(OUT/'preparation-costs.json');text+=f'Preparation elapsed at freeze: {p["elapsed_seconds"]/60:.1f} minutes. Measured shared-gate CPU and focused test timings are retained separately; unmetered interactive work is not assigned invented compute hours.\n\n'
 text+='Evidence: [registration](../experiments/'+RUN+'/registration.json), [folds](../experiments/'+RUN+'/folds.json), [input hashes](../experiments/'+RUN+'/input-manifest.json), [shared validation](../experiments/'+RUN+'/shared-validation-summary.json), [source hashes](../experiments/'+RUN+'/source-manifest.json), [literature notes](../experiments/'+RUN+'/literature-adaptation.md), [analysis](../experiments/'+RUN+'/analysis.json), [completion/cost](../experiments/'+RUN+'/completion.json).\n'
 REPORT.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8');status=R/'docs/STATUS.md';old=status.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');start='<!-- BELIEF-BAYES001 -->';end='<!-- BELIEF-BAYES001-END -->'
 if start in old:i=old.index(start);j=old.index(end,i)+len(end);old=old[:i]+old[j:].lstrip('\n')
 status.write_text(f'{start}\n## Bayesian deck inference + conditional allocation\n\n{iso()}: **{state}**. {reason} Frozen4-fold/3-inner-fold development comparison; no held-out/native/GPU/neural/PPO work. [Report](../reports/astra-unown-belief-bayesian-deck-inference.md).\n{end}\n\n'+old,encoding='utf-8')
 mirror=Path('C:/path/to/ptcg-agent') if os.name=='nt' else Path('/path/to/ptcg-agent')
 for source in [REPORT,status]+[p for p in OUT.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ('.json','.jsonl','.md')]+list((OUT/'model-selection').glob('*.json')):
  target=mirror/source.relative_to(R);target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copy2(source,target)
